{"type":"text","timestamp":1786048189818,"sessionID":"ses_0273c7954ffexy9LoZ6Jbws1Be","part":{"id":"prt_fd8c48fd3001wkaju1rduLTQQK","messageID":"msg_fd8c48548001Z9SArV0pYIiCvm","sessionID":"ses_0273c7954ffexy9LoZ6Jbws1Be","type":"text","text":"I have successfully created all three required files for your new candidate model:\n\n1. **`hypothesis.md`**: I've defined a specific hypothesis focused on **run-length entropy**. It argues that people expect a truly random sequence to have a diverse distribution of streak lengths, and compares this to a subjective ideal. This sharply disagrees with the incumbent model by naturally penalizing periodic or overly structured sequences (like `HHTTHHTT`) that have a normal run count but zero run-length diversity.\n2. **`model_name.txt`**: The model is named `run_length_entropy`.\n3. **`candidate.py`**: I've translated the hypothesis into a PyMC model. The module includes a custom `compute_features` function that extracts the Shannon entropy of each sequence's run-length distribution. The model fits two cognitive parameters: an `ideal_entropy` (the subjective target diversity) and `tau` (the choice steepness), scoring sequences based on their quadratic distance from this ideal entropy.\n\nThe self-check passes and the pipeline will be able to load the model and map the data columns.","time":{"start":1786048188371,"end":1786048189816}}}
